Five foundation models now receive the input their authors trained them on. They were all fed plain microvolts before, so their embeddings and fine-tunes change and must be recomputed. The convention of each model is read from its authors' code, is declared on `FoundationModelSpec` (`input_reference`, `input_scale`, `input_normalization`, `input_clip`, `finetune_input_scale`), is applied by the backend for embeddings and for fine-tuning, and is recorded with the embeddings:

  - LaBraM: units of 100 µV (`/ 100` in the tokenizer, pretraining and fine-tuning engines).
  - BIOT: each bipolar channel of a window divided by the 95th percentile of its absolute value.
  - LUNA: each channel of a window z-scored, and resampling to 256 Hz instead of 200 Hz.
  - REVE: each channel of a window z-scored and clipped to ±15 when the backbone is frozen (embeddings, linear probe), as in pretraining; units of 100 µV when the backbone is trained, as in the authors' downstream code. The authors z-score with the statistics of a whole recording; the backend only sees a window. The REVE backend applied no input convention at all before.
  - EEGPT: average reference over the channels it keeps, millivolts, and resampling to 256 Hz instead of 250 Hz. The authors' own downstream code does not use one scale; this follows their pretraining data preparation.

The eight foundation models are no longer pinned to a checkpoint revision: each load takes the latest revision of its Hugging Face repository (the pinned ones were the latest, apart from documentation commits on REVE). `backend_kwargs={"revision": ...}` still selects one.

BENDR's classification head is trained on the mean of its time tokens, the features `transform()` returns. braindecode feeds the head the transformer output at the start token, which is almost the same for every input on the released checkpoint, so linear probes and LoRA fine-tunes stayed at chance.

`transform()` and `predict()` of a foundation backend now run in evaluation mode. After a fit without a validation split the model was left in training mode, so both ran with dropout on.
